      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be the first player to reach the target score (often 5000) by melding sets and runs and going out; opponents add deadwood to your score.',
      'Turn-flow example: Deal full hands. Turn: draw one (from stock or multiple from discard pile, per variant), meld sets/runs if desired, discard one. Going out ends the round; others count deadwood against them. Round scores (or penalties) accumulate; first to target wins.',
      'Scoring example: Melded cards score points: aces and wild cards are typically worth 100 points each (or 200 when aces are wild); other picture cards and tens are 10 points; numeral cards 2–9 are 5 points. Unmelded cards left in hand at the end of a hand count against the player, and going out may award a bonus. Target score is often 5000, but many groups use 1500, 2000, 2200, 2500, 2800 or 10000. Be the first player to reach the target score (often 5000) by melding sets and runs and going out; opponents add deadwood to your score..',
